From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: Do not self-update the managed daemon from chatgpt.com by default

The packaged app-server daemon (daemon_auto_start, on by default since 0.157.0)
spawns an updater that, five minutes after start and then hourly, downloads
https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh, runs it, and swaps the RPM-installed
binary for an upstream prebuilt in ~/.codex/packages/app-server-daemon.  Updates
come from the package manager here, so default the daemon updater to off; users
who want it can set updater.autoUpdateEnabled = true in
~/.codex/app-server-daemon/settings.json.

Downstream-only distribution policy, not suitable for upstream submission.

--- a/codex-rs/app-server-daemon/src/settings.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/app-server-daemon/src/settings.rs
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
         Self {
             remote_control_enabled: false,
             feature_overrides: BTreeMap::new(),
-            auto_update_enabled: true,
+            auto_update_enabled: false,
             update_interval_minutes: DEFAULT_UPDATE_INTERVAL_MINUTES,
             shutdown_grace_seconds: DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS,
         }
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 }
 
 fn default_auto_update_enabled() -> bool {
-    true
+    false
 }
 
 fn default_update_interval_minutes() -> u32 {
